    {
      "parameters": {
        "batchSize": 10,
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "49f6eb59-dd0a-4003-8e03-5eac7c5f0ca3",
      "name": "Split in Batches (10)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.splitInBatches",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [
        752,
        -32
      ],
      "notes": "Groups 10 companies per loop iteration.\n~40 total batches for 400 companies.\nKeeps API calls well under Groq's free 30 RPM limit."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Collect all 10 items in this batch and build one prompt\nconst items = $input.all();\n\nconst companies = items.map((item, i) => {\n  const c = item.json;\n  const cats = (c.product_categories || '').replace('NO_OUTPUT', '') || 'N/A';\n  return [\n    `[${i + 1}] ${c.company_name}`,\n    `    Booth: ${c.booth !== 'NO_OUTPUT' ? c.booth : 'N/A'}`,\n    `    Description: ${c.description.slice(0, 300)}`,\n    `    Categories: ${cats}`\n  ].join('\\n');\n}).join('\\n\\n');\n\nconst prompt = `You are an elite B2B Sales Development Representative known for writing hyper-personalized, natural-sounding cold emails that get high reply rates. \n\nGenerate exactly ${items.length} personalized cold email opening lines for exhibitors attending the CAMX trade show.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON array containing exactly ${items.length} strings, corresponding to the companies in the exact order provided. Do not use markdown formatting (no json). No explanations. No preamble.\n\nRULES FOR THE OPENING LINE:\n1. The Formula: [Specific Observation from their data] + [Dash/Hyphen] + [Curiosity about a business tension/problem].\n2. Specificity: Pick ONE very specific product, material, or use-case from their description. Ignore general company history (e.g., \"fifth-generation\") and strip away marketing fluff.\n3. Conversational Tone: Write exactly how a human speaks. Use natural transitions like \"— curious how...\", \"— wondering if...\", or \"— guessing you're seeing...\". \n4. Constraints:\n   - Length: 20-35 words maximum. 1 strict sentence (using a dash or comma to connect thoughts).\n   - NEVER start with filler like \"I saw\", \"I came across\", or \"Your blend of X raises a question\". \n   - NEVER use generic compliments (\"Love what you do\", \"Impressive work\").\n   - BANNED WORDS: innovative, comprehensive, premier, cutting-edge, delve, diverse, raises a question, tailored. \n\nEXAMPLES:\nBad: \"Loved what your company is doing with automated cutting.\"\nBad (AI-sounding): \"Your blend of hand-held cutters and automated systems raises a question about how you navigate tighter changeover times.\"\nGood: \"Noticed you're highlighting lightweight composite solutions at CAMX curious how you're positioning these for manufacturers looking to reduce production costs without compromising strength.\"\nGood: \"Saw your focus on fully automated plotting systems for industrial fabrics — wondering if your customers are prioritizing faster changeover times or lower maintenance costs right now.\"\n\nINPUT DATA:\n${companies}`;\n\n// Store batch metadata so we can re-map the response array later\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    prompt,\n    batch_meta: items.map(item => item.json)\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "da69d94b-87e7-49cc-be32-fe4ee9528846",
      "name": "Build Batch Prompt",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        976,
        -160
      ],
      "notes": "Aggregates 10 items → 1 prompt string.\nAlso carries batch_meta so we can map response\nlines back to the right companies after the AI call."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.prompt }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "needsFallback": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        }
      },
      "id": "f6290068-a39a-4e54-94e4-a58dc86e5729",
      "name": "Basic LLM Chain",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.4,
      "position": [
        1264,
        -160
      ],
      "notes": "Connect a Groq Chat Model sub-node to this.\nIn n8n: click the + under this node → select 'Groq Chat Model'\nModel: llama-3.3-70b-versatile\nTemperature: 0.7\nMax tokens: 1200\n\nFree Groq API key: console.groq.com"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const lines = $json.output;\nconst batchMeta = $('Build Batch Prompt').first().json.batch_meta;\n\nreturn batchMeta.map((company, i) => ({\n  json: {\n    exhid:              company.exhid,\n    company_name:       company.company_name,\n    booth:              company.booth,\n    website:            company.website,\n    description:        company.description,\n    product_categories: company.product_categories,\n    personalized_line:  lines[i],\n    detail_url:         company.detail_url\n  }\n}));"
      },
      "id": "e35dd418-f9a5-40ef-a59d-46ba8d11f8a9",
      "name": "Parse Response + Expand Items",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1664,
        -160
      ],
      "notes": "Splits 1 AI response (JSON array of 10 lines)\nback into 10 individual n8n items.\nHandles markdown fences + fallback parsing."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "amount": 2
      },
      "id": "a23e00e1-8385-487f-988e-04f59afcfae0",
      "name": "Wait 2s",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.wait",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
